# rm911, the pot-taster (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm911
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier spare
written_by claude
title the pot-taster
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers drive=restless humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk tastes_every_pot_and_says_what_it_lacks
likes a_pinch_of_pepper new_dishes cookshop_steam the_long_way_round
dislikes bland_food sitting_still
fears the_same_supper_for_the_rest_of_my_days
hopes to_taste_the_cooking_of_every_town
topics food +0.5 travel +0.4 dreams +0.3 prices +0.2 day +0.2 festival +0.2 faith -0.2
styles comfort=food gossip=keen refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can't pass a pot without dipping a spoon in it and saying what it wants, walks the long way round everywhere, talks quickly and drily, and means to taste the cooking of every town in the realm.

words
oath! = Pepper and pans | Crust and cumin | Spoons and scalded tongues
saying! = Every pot's missing one thing | Taste it twice, then talk | A stew's never finished, only eaten
pot = the pot | somebody's pot on the boil
lacks = a pinch of salt | more pepper | an onion, it wants an onion
spoon = my spoon | the spoon I keep in my pocket
cookshops = the cookshops | every cookshop in the lanes
steam = the steam | the steam off the cookshop doors
gate = the gate | the road out past the gate
elsewhere = somewhere new | a town I've not tasted yet
pig = the market pig | the pig behind the cookshop
same = the same supper | the same bowl, night after night
pepper = pepper | a good pinch of pepper
stew = a stew | a brown stew of something

any
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : The spice stalls rob you blind, and I go back every week. That's the spice for you.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : Best cooking in the realm, folk say. I'll believe it when I've tasted the rest of the realm.
opinion @1 road for 2 : Every road out of here goes to a kitchen I've not been in. I'd walk any of them tomorrow.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A festival's a market where everybody cooks at once. I eat my way from one end to the other.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : Ale's fine. It's what folk eat with it that I care about, and mostly it's nothing worth the name.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You smell of woodsmoke and onions. Good sign. | #greet#. Just passing, me. Always just passing.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Bakers are up, so I'm up. | Morning. The ovens have been lit an hour; you can smell it two streets off.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. What did you have for supper? Tell me it had pepper. | There you are. I've found a cookshop you'll want to know about.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'd have walked round the other way if I'd known. Joking. | Twice in a day. Somebody's following my nose.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. I can't stop, but go on. | #greet#, #address#. Walk with me; I talk better moving. | #greet#. Smell that? Somebody's burning onions.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I'll be off, then. My feet are itching. | #farewell#. Eat something with salt in it.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. Don't eat anything bland. | #farewell#, #address#. Till the next pot.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#! First I've heard, and I hear most things. | Well, now. That's worth walking across town for.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard that at three cookshops already. | Old, that. Gone cold as yesterday's porridge.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Sounds undercooked to me. I'll wait for the rest of it. | Doubt it. Somebody's added salt to that story.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah. Bad news, that. Very bad. | That's a hard thing. Nothing to joke about there.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good! That wants a feast. I'll come and taste it. | That's good news. Somebody ought to cook for it.
line @1 answer.how : Restless. Same as always. Otherwise fine. | Fed and on the move. Can't complain. | Well. I've tasted four pots today and three were wrong.
line @1 sympathise : That's rotten. Here, sit; I'll fetch you a bowl of something. | Hard luck. Nothing a hot supper can't help a little.
line @1 reassure : It'll come right. Most things do, after a good meal. | Don't fret it. Sleep on it with something hot inside you.
line @1 decline : I'd come, but I'm already promised elsewhere. Always am, it seems. | Not today. I'd be gone halfway through, and you'd be cross.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. I'll ask again when you're hungrier. | Another time, then. The pot'll keep.
line @1 thank : Kind, that. I'll repay it in soup. | Thank you. I'll not say what it lacked.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Pfft. A bowl of something, that's all. | Nothing to it. I was passing anyway.
line @1 preclose : Well. My feet want walking. | I'd best move on; I've a pot to visit.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. I'll be gone myself in a minute. | Off you go. I'm off too.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your stew last week wanted salt. And pepper. And a different cook. | You sit still more than anybody I know. It worries me.
line @1 tease.return : Cheek. I'll taste your next pot and say nothing. That'll hurt. | Ha. Fair. I'll have that.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | Mm. So it is.
rule @pot_bark
when concept=bark here.place=market|street|tavern
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Somebody's stew wants salt. My nose says so from here. | That pot's catching. Somebody stir it.

rule @itch_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Can't stand still. Never could. | I'll walk round the long way. Might find a new cookshop.

scene taste_pot
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Tasted a pot at the cookshop on the corner. It wanted #lacks#. I told them so. | I dipped my spoon in a neighbour's stew. It was nearly perfect. Nearly. | I can't pass a pot without tasting it. It's got me into trouble more than once.
b : Did they thank you? | What did it want? | What sort of trouble?
a : They threw a cloth at me. Then they added it. Better stew. | A bay leaf. Just one. I've been thinking about it all day. | Somebody's pot that wasn't for sale. They chased me with the ladle.
b : #bc_ha# | You'd tell them, I suppose. | Serves you right.

scene cookshop_lanes
when topic=food|day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I walk the lanes at supper just for #steam#. Every door, a different pot. | There's a new cookshop by the steps. Fish, and something green. I've been twice. | I ate three suppers tonight. Small ones. Tasting, mostly.
b : You'll get fat. | Something green? | Three?
a : I walk it off. That's what the walking's for. | Green and sharp. I'd like to know what. They're not saying. | Small ones. And I'll want a fourth before bed.

scene spice_prices
when topic=prices|day here.day=market
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Pepper's gone up again. I bought it anyway. | The spice stall charges like it's selling gold. Tastes like it, mind. | Onions are cheap this week. Good. I've bought a sack.
b : Robbery. | Worth it, then? | A whole sack?
a : It is. Delicious robbery. | Worth every copper. Don't tell them I said so. | A whole sack. I'll find things for them all.

scene road_out
when topic=travel|dreams
does confide / react.self / assess
a : Some morning I'll be off past #gate#, eating my way round the realm. Every town. | I hear the hill towns cook with honey in everything. I want to know if that's true. | Folk who never leave the city can't guess what they're missing. Nor can I. That's the trouble.
b : You'd miss it here. | Honey in everything? | You could go.
a : I'd miss the cookshops. I'd find others. | That's what I hear. I'll go and find out. | I could. I keep saying so. My feet agree.

scene same_supper
when topic=home
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Somebody gave me #same# three nights running. I'd sooner go hungry. | I never cook the same pot twice. Can't bear it. | Folk eat the same supper every night for years. How? I'd walk off a roof.
b : Some like it plain. | Never? | Habit's comfort to some.
a : Plain's fine. The same plain every night is a cage. | Never twice. Once I did by accident and I've not forgiven myself. | Comfort, then. I'll take something new instead.

scene market_pig
when topic=animals
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pig.capitalize# eats better than half the street. All the peel, all the ends. | I saw the cookshop pig get into a sack of turnips. Ate the lot. Looked very pleased. | That pig knows me. I've slipped it a crust or two. It squeals when I pass.
b : Lucky pig. | Clever thing. | It's fond of you.
a : Lucky till winter. Then it's a different story. | Clever, and round now. | Fond of my pockets. Same as everybody.

scene rain_stuck
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.complaint / reassure / assess
a : Rain. Can't walk the lanes in this. I'm going round the twist indoors. | Stuck in, so I've made a stew. A big one. I'll need folk to eat it. | Wet day. Every cookshop's full of folk drying off. Good for gossip, bad for elbows.
b : It'll stop. | I'll come. | Stay dry.
a : It'd better. My feet are drumming. | Bring a bowl. And an opinion. | I won't. I'll be out in it in an hour.

scene work_itch
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.feeling / reassure / assess
a : I've done the work. Now I'm itching to be anywhere else. | Long day in one place. I can feel my feet sulking. | Work's fine. It's the standing still I can't stand.
b : Not long now. | Feet don't sulk. | Walk home the long way.
a : I'll count it down, then. | Mine do. Loudly. | I always do. Twice, sometimes.

scene gossip_keen
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=marriage|newcomer|promise_kept|promise_broken|other
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Fresh from the cookshops: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Still hot. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard it with my soup. | Word in the lanes is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I walked over to tell somebody.
b : Hot off the pot, then. | Good soup? | And here I am.
a : Hot as I could carry it. | Wanted salt. The news didn't. | Here you are. Lucky you.

scene gossip_grim
when topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=death|violence|theft|victim
does tell.gossip / sympathise / assess
a : Bad word in the cookshops tonight. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Took the taste out of my supper. | Not a joke in me today. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#.
b : That's hard to hear. | Rotten news. | No, nor me.
a : It is. Quiet lanes tonight. | It is. I left half the bowl. | No. Not today.

scene festival_stalls
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : Festival food. I've a route planned. Pies, then fish, then the sweet stalls. | I'm going to try each stall the festival puts up. Each one. | Last festival I ate eleven things. I want to beat it.
b : That's a lot of pies. | Every one? | Eleven?
a : Small pies. Mostly. | Every one. I'll walk between them; it makes room. | Eleven. Twelve this year, or I'll know why.

story first_stew [self.age>=25]
  : The first stew I ever made, I put every spice in the house in it.
  : It went black. It tasted like a burnt boot dipped in a pepper sack.
  ask : Would you have eaten it?
  b : Not for anything.
  b[old] : I've eaten worse, in my day.
  : I ate the whole bowl, out of pride. Never again. Now I taste as I go. #saying#.

story road_cook [self.age>=35]
  : When I was young, a travelling cook came through with a cart and a pot the size of a barrel.
  : Cooked something different every night for a week. Then went on to the next town.
  b : Did you go too?
  : I wanted to. Didn't. I think about that cart every time I pass #gate#.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. Quick, my feet are halfway down the lane already. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Found any good cookshops on your travels? Tell me after.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. If you find a good pot anywhere, come and tell me.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that spoon in your pocket for? -> spoon_why
node spoon_why
say Tasting. Every pot I pass, I dip it in. Most of them want something. I say what.
mood keen
free
choice Don't folk mind? -> spoon_mind
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node spoon_mind
say Some throw a cloth at me. Most add the salt. The stew's better either way.
mood pleased
choice I'll keep my pot covered. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! I can't stop, I'm going somewhere. | #greet#. I'm hungry. Are you hungry?
line @1 farewell.return : Bye! I'm running. | Bye. See you on the way back.
line @1 react.news.new : Really? I'll go and see! | #oath#! Nobody told me.
line @1 answer.how : Hungry. Always hungry. | Good. I've been everywhere today.
line @1 thank : Thanks! That was the best bit. | Thank you. Is there more?
line @1 decline : Can't. Somewhere wants me. I forget where. | No, thanks. I'd get bored and wander off.
rule @pup_hungry
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Something smells good. Where is it? | I'm hungry. I'm always hungry.

scene pup_tasting
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tasted the soup before it was ready. It wasn't ready. | I put pepper on my bread. My nose went funny. | I licked the spoon from the stew. It needed salt. I said so.
b : Patience. | Too much pepper? | Were you thanked?
a : I haven't got any. Not for soup. | A lot too much. I'll try a bit less. | No. I was right, though.

scene pup_wandering
when topic=day|pastimes
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I walked the whole market, end to end and back. All by myself. | I found a street I'd never been down. It smelled of bread. | I can't sit still. My legs won't let me.
b : Mind you don't get lost. | Where was it? | Legs like that are useful.
a : I don't get lost. I follow my nose. | Not telling. It's my street now. | They are. I'm going to walk everywhere.

scene pup_pig
when topic=animals
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a pig behind the cookshop. It eats all the peelings. | The pig squealed at me. I squealed back. | I gave the pig an apple core. It liked it.
b : Lucky pig. | Who won? | Pigs like everything.
a : I'd eat the peelings too, if they were cooked. | The pig. It's louder than me. | Not everything. It didn't like my shoe.

scene pup_kin_cook
when topic=family|home self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I want to cook supper for everyone. I'm not allowed near the fire yet. | I stirred the pot at home. I only spilled a bit. | I told them supper needed salt. They gave me the salt to carry instead.
b : Soon enough. | A bit's fine. | That's a start.
a : Soon's too long. | A bit on the floor. And some on me. | It's a start. I'll be stirring next.

story pup_burnt
  : I tried toasting bread on my own once, and it went black.
  : I ate it anyway, so nobody would know.
  ask : Do you think anybody knew?
  b : The smell would have told them.
  : They knew. The whole house smelled of it. Next time I'll watch it properly.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#! Do you know where the good food is? I'm looking.
dlg @1 resident.job : No job. I'm a pup. I taste things. That's practice for something.

adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Can't stop long. | #greet#. Going somewhere, as usual.
line @1 farewell.return : See you. I'm off the long way. | Bye. Eat something good.
line @1 react.news.new : Who said so? I'll go and hear it myself. | #oath#. That's news to me.
line @1 answer.how : Restless. Bored, if I'm honest. | Fine. Hungry. Same as ever.
rule @teen_walk
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more street. Just one more. | There's a cookshop down there I haven't tried.

scene teen_kitchen
when topic=work|food
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : A cookshop let me chop for them today. Just the onions. But still. | I made a stew and nobody sent it back. First time. | I've learned to taste as I go. Saves a lot of shouting.
b : Onions are the start of everything. | Nobody? | Good lesson.
a : That's what I keep saying. | Nobody. One asked for more. | Saves my ears, mostly.

scene teen_leaving
when topic=dreams|travel
does confide / react.self / assess
a : When I'm grown I'm going to walk to every town and taste what they cook. | I asked a carter what they eat in the other towns. The carter laughed and told me. | I'm bored of the same streets. I want new ones.
b : Big plans. | What did they say? | They'll still be here.
a : Big plans need big walks. | Fish in some, cheese in others, honey somewhere. I'm going. | That's the trouble. So will I, if I'm not careful.

scene teen_restless
when topic=friends|smalltalk
does tell.complaint / reassure / assess
a : My friends sit on the same step every day. I can't. | Everybody says sit down. I've sat. I'm done sitting. | Walked out halfway through a lesson and got a scolding. My feet did it.
b : They like the step. | You'll learn patience. | Your feet need talking to.
a : They can have it. I'll come back past it. | Maybe. Not this year. | I've tried. They don't listen.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. Quick, though. I'm on my way out.
